course: dictionary
lesson: 1612
title: Chef and its plural
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A chef is a person whose job is to cook, often the main cook in a restaurant or hotel. Context gives you clues: «Carbon steel knives get dark spots when left wet, so chefs dry them at once» tells you chefs work in a kitchen with knives and wet food.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Lionfish... chefs cook them to help reefs» still makes sense if you say «cooks cook them», so a chef is a cook.
explain: Notice the plural. Chef becomes chefs by adding just -s. Many words ending in -f or -fe change to -ves, like knife and knives, but chef follows the -s rule, like roofs.
fact: A chef is a person whose job is to cook.
fact: A head chef leads the other cooks in a kitchen.
fact: The plural of chef is chefs: just add -s.
fact: «Only chefs with a special licence may prepare fugu», because parts of the pufferfish hold a very strong poison.
fact: Chefs keep food and kitchens safe by washing their hands and drying their knives at once.
exercise: What is a chef? | A person who sells food in the street | *A person whose job is to cook | A machine that washes plates | A sharp knife used in a kitchen
exercise: What does a head chef do? | Washes the dishes at the sink | Grows vegetables on a farm | *Leads the other cooks in a kitchen | Sells tickets at the cinema
exercise: Which is the correct plural of chef? | *chefs | chiefs | chefves | cheves
test: In «so chefs dry them at once», what does chefs mean? | Divers who hunt fish | Wet kitchen floors | *People whose job is to cook | Sharp metal tools
test: Which plural just adds -s and does not change to -ves? | knives | leaves | *chefs | loaves
exam: In «only trained chefs may prepare them», who may prepare the fish? | Anyone who likes fish | Children | *Trained cooks | Divers and fishers
